{"code": "import math\n\ndef predict(probe):\n    # Mechanism inferred from the evidence:\n    #\n    # 1. There is a special point at x = 0.0: f(0) = 1548.92 [E2, E18, E24].\n    #\n    # 2. For x > 0 (positive side):\n    #    - Very small positive x gives about -11.4, not -12.4. The switch from\n    #      -11.4 to -12.4 happens between x = 0.01 (gives -11.4) and x = 0.1\n    #      (gives -11.4) ... wait: E4 shows 0.01,0.1,0.9,1.0,2.0 all -11.4,\n    #      and 4.0 gives -11.4, 4.1 gives -11.4, 4.2 gives -12.4.\n    #      E10: 4.1 -> -11.4, 4.2..4.9 -> -12.4. So positive side is -11.4\n    #      for 0 < x < ~4.15, then -12.4 for larger x.\n    #      Boundary: between 4.1 and 4.2 (E10), and E14 shows 4.14 -> -12.4,\n    #      4.16 -> -12.4. So boundary ~4.15? E14 has 4.14 already -12.4.\n    #      E10: 4.1 -> -11.4, 4.2 -> -12.4. So boundary in (4.1, 4.2).\n    #      E14: 4.14 -> -12.4, so boundary in (4.1, 4.14].\n    #      Use 4.12? E20 has 4.13 -> -12.4. So boundary <= 4.13.\n    #      Best guess: threshold at 4.12 (between 4.1 and 4.13). ? \n    #      Actually E14 has 4.14 -> -12.4, E20 has 4.13 -> -12.4,\n    #      E10 has 4.1 -> -11.4. So boundary in (4.1, 4.13].\n    #      I'll pick 4.12 as the cutoff. ?\n    #\n    # 3. For x < 0 (negative side):\n    #    - Very small negative x gives +9.8.\n    #    - Around x = -4.1 the value drops from 9.8 to 8.8.\n    #      E8: -4.0 -> 9.8, -4.5 -> 8.8. E12: -4.1 -> 9.8, -4.15 -> 8.8.\n    #      E16: -4.08 -> 9.8, -4.12 -> 8.8. E22: -4.105 -> 9.8,\n    #      -4.11 -> 8.8. So boundary between -4.105 and -4.11.\n    #      Use -4.108? E22: -4.105 -> 9.8, -4.11 -> 8.8.\n    #      Boundary in (-4.11, -4.105]. Pick -4.108. ?\n    #    - For x more negative than that (x < ~-4.108), the value is 8.8,\n    #      until a second boundary where it becomes -12.4.\n    #      E2: -5.0 -> 8.8, -15.0 -> 8.8, -30.0 -> 8.8, -100 -> 8.8.\n    #      E20: -8 -> 8.8, -16 -> 8.8, -64 -> 8.8, -128 -> 8.8.\n    #      Wait,